{"id":"01M4GAJW01452CK86RNE2AJ9N6","t":2,"a":"83a1","op":"set","k":"description","v":"Legacy: `siren-board-slice/03` (`.scratch/siren-board-slice/03-migrate-step-reveal-demo.md`)\nSpec: `01M4GAJVP4C3KGZSECWJVZ83R5`\nCommits: `9decc49`\n\n---\n\n# 03 Migrate demos/step-reveal.html onto @siren/board\n\n## Outcome\n\n`demos/step-reveal.html` renders and behaves exactly as it does today, but its\n`<script type=\"module\">` block now just fetches the `.srn` source and calls `createBoard` — the\nhand-rolled canvas text measurer, theme-toggle-adjacent control wiring, and diagnostics/error\nhandling that block used to contain are deleted, replaced by `@siren/board`'s built-in equivalents\nwired through `onStepChange`/`onDiagnostics`.\n\nNote: `demos/demo-chrome.css`'s `#siren-container`/`.controls` rules are shared with\n`complex-showcase.html`, which is not migrated until ticket 04 — do not remove those rules from\n`demo-chrome.css` in this ticket, or `complex-showcase.html` breaks until ticket 04 lands. This\nticket only edits `step-reveal.html`'s own markup/script and, if needed, adds new rules — it does\nnot delete the shared ones.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `demos/step-reveal.html` imports `@siren/board`'s built build output (`packages/board/dist/…`,\n      not source files — matching the existing convention of importing `@siren/core`'s built\n      `dist/siren-core.js`, never source, per ticket 07's precedent in\n      `.scratch/siren-core-step-reveal-slice/`).\n- [ ] The page's hand-rolled `createBrowserTextMeasurer()`, the `themeBtn`-adjacent control button\n      wiring for Prev/Next/Reset (Theme stays as page-owned code — board has no theme concept),\n      and the `svg === null` / diagnostics console-warning block are deleted from the page's\n      script; `board`'s defaults and `onDiagnostics`/`onStepChange` callbacks replace them.\n- [ ] The static `<div class=\"controls\">` markup for Prev/Next/Reset buttons is deleted from the\n      HTML (board renders its own); the Theme button (and its own click handler) stays, since\n      theming remains this page's own concern.\n- [ ] The `<p class=\"status\" id=\"status\">Step 0 of 0</p>` element's text is now updated via\n      `options.onStepChange`, not via manual `updateStatus()` calls after each button click.\n- [ ] Visually verified (headless-Chrome screenshot, matching the method used for the earlier\n      full-bleed layout change): the page looks and behaves the same as before this ticket — full-\n      bleed canvas, floating control bar, intro/status text at top, dark-theme toggle still works.\n- [ ] `pnpm --filter @siren/core build && pnpm --filter @siren/board build`, then serving the repo\n      root over http(s) and loading the page, produces no console errors and a working\n      Prev/Next/Reset/Theme cycle.\n\n## Test seam\n\nManual/visual verification (headless Chrome screenshot + `console --errors`-equivalent check via\nChrome's console output), as used for the full-bleed layout change earlier in this project — this\nis a demo page, not a unit under `@siren/board`'s own test seam. `@siren/board`'s own behavior is\nalready covered by tickets 01/02's automated tests; this ticket proves real integration, not new\nboard behavior.\n\n## Write ownership\n\n- `demos/step-reveal.html`\n- `demos/demo-chrome.css` (additive/adjusted rules only — no deletion of `#siren-container`/`.controls`, see Outcome note)\n\n## Shared resources\n\nA local static server on a free port (e.g. `python3 -m http.server`) for manual verification —\nstop it after use; don't leave it running across tickets.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n02 (needs the default control bar, `onStepChange`, and `onDiagnostics` to exist).\n\n## Status\n\ndone (commit 9decc49)\n\n## Done when\n\n- A failing behavior test was observed before implementation, per acceptance criterion (for the\n  automated parts; the visual criteria are verified by screenshot, not a test file).\n- `pnpm -r test` and relevant static checks pass.\n- Manual visual verification screenshot taken and reviewed.\n- Standards and spec review blockers are resolved."}
